The built web app (proseway/static) bundles React, ReactDOM and scheduler (MIT) and the
fonts Literata, Source Serif 4, Atkinson Hyperlegible Next and OpenDyslexic (SIL Open Font
License 1.1). Their licence texts are reproduced in proseway/static/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt.

Python dependencies are not bundled; your package manager installs them under their own
licences: FastAPI (MIT), Starlette (BSD-3-Clause), Uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause), python-multipart
(Apache-2.0), pdfplumber and pdfminer.six (MIT), pypdfium2 (Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause, with
PDFium under BSD-3-Clause and other permissive licences), psutil (BSD-3-Clause), RapidFuzz
(MIT) and segno (BSD-3-Clause). The optional OCR add-on uses RapidOCR (Apache-2.0) with
ONNX Runtime (MIT).

The full licence review is in docs/research/licenses.md in the source repository.
